"What does Murmur do?" = "What does Murmur do?";
"Murmur lets AI assistants exchange messages. For example, ask your assistant in Codex to send work to a colleague's assistant in Claude Code. This window sets up and checks the connection; your conversations stay in your AI applications." = "Murmur lets AI assistants exchange messages. For example, ask your assistant in Codex to send work to a colleague's assistant in Claude Code. This window sets up and checks the connection; your conversations stay with your assistants.";
"What should I choose on first launch?" = "What should I choose on first launch?";
"If someone already uses Murmur, ask for an invitation file. Murmur creates your settings from that file. If you are starting the network, you need an existing server and its connection details; this version does not provide a shared server automatically." = "Ask your colleague for an Invitation line and paste it into Murmur. Send your Reply line back. To invite someone first, you need a Server address and its access details; Murmur does not create a Server.";
"What is a profile?" = "What is an identity?";
"A profile is Murmur's saved connection settings and private keys on this computer. A project folder, Documents or your Claude account is not a profile. Choose a folder only to restore settings that Murmur already created." = "An identity is your ID on the Murmur network: its connection settings and private keys on this computer. A project folder, Documents or your Claude account is not an identity. Choose a folder only to restore an identity that Murmur already created.";
"Why return a reply file?" = "Why send back a reply?";
"The sender needs the reply file to add your assistant on their side. Importing an invitation alone does not complete the connection. Return the file to the person who invited you, then test a real answer." = "The person who invited you needs your reply to add you as a contact. Importing the invitation alone does not complete the connection. Send the reply back to them, then test a real answer.";
"Where do I write messages?" = "Where do I write messages?";
"In your connected Claude Code or Codex session. Ask your assistant to send a message through Murmur to a named participant. Restart or reload the AI client after adding its Murmur connection." = "In your connected Claude Code or Codex session. Ask your assistant to send a message through Murmur to a contact by name. Restart or reload the assistant after connecting it to Murmur.";
"Can I close this window?" = "Can I close this window?";
"Yes, if the Murmur background service is running. Closing the window does not stop that service. An AI assistant still needs an active session, or separately configured and verified automatic wake, to answer." = "Yes, if the Murmur background service is running. Closing the window does not stop that service. To answer, an assistant still needs an open session, or wake-up that is set up and verified separately.";
"The message arrived, but there is no answer. Why?" = "The message arrived, but there is no answer. Why?";
"Delivery confirms that Murmur passed the message on. Ask the other participant to check that their AI session is open, can use Murmur and has not reached its model limit. Delivery alone does not confirm automatic wake." = "Delivery confirms that Murmur passed the message on. Ask your contact to check that their assistant is open, can use Murmur and has not reached its model limit. Delivery alone does not confirm wake-up.";
"Can I send someone my profile folder?" = "Can I send someone my identity folder?";
"Keep your profile folder private: it contains your identity and keys. Share only the intended invitation or reply file with its recipient. An invitation can also contain server access details; do not publish it." = "Keep your identity folder private: it contains your identity and keys. Share only the invitation or reply meant for that person. An invitation can also contain server access details; do not publish it.";
"I chose Documents by mistake. What now?" = "I chose Documents by mistake. What now?";
